        [ dct:description "The ETSI TR 103 290 specification focuses on ensuring that data generated across diverse platforms can be collected, transmitted, and processed effectively, enabling interoperability and meaningful use of the information. In this sense, it provides guidance on how data exchange should be handled to support Smart City applications."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataExchangeApplicationService ],
        [ dct:description "The ETSI TR 103 290 specification is designed to define the activities occurring within a smart city, in the context of the Internet of Things (IoT). Among other elements, the specification presents various use cases and introduces terminology relevant to the smart city domain."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:ControlledVocabularyDataObject ],
        [ dct:description "ETSI TR 103 290 focuses on how Smart City and IoT systems can handle and process large volumes of raw data from connected devices. It outlines requirements and best practices for turning this data into actionable insights for urban services. The goal is to enable informed decision-making, such as improving traffic flow, reducing pollution, or optimising energy use."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:AnalyticsTechnologyService ] ;
    dcat:theme "Data Architecture"@en,
        "Technology Architecture"@en .

cssvrsc:09d5f955aa3f2e89a91b884839963a35be68332c58006c53d8d7f88e882cb4fa a cssv:Specification ;
    dct:relation [ dct:description "CPOV provides a simplified, reusable and extensible data model to give structure and format for the structure of a public organisation."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataModelDataObject ],
        [ dct:description "CPOV supplies a common semantic model for describing public organisations, their structures, roles, and relationships. It facilitates harmonised representation of public administration entities across Member States, enabling interoperability in registries, public-sector directories, service descriptions, and organisational metadata. As a foundational vocabulary, it can be extended or profiled to meet national or sector-specific requirements while ensuring compatibility with broader European interoperability efforts."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:VocabularyDataObject ],
        camssa:25a391b815d1366d9abbd182f846ef1953956c6ff4460c7a6741d114ee3a8fb3,
        camssa:4d275ba63d9fc120129b7025cd8826c702866a10b710bb8c8f46d5d43bcf0c1b ;
    dcat:theme "Data Architecture"@en .

cssvrsc:0b20d84fe402cde345d199f82abee4c0c80ba0b54a8af80aab8ce982cef2692d a cssv:Specification ;
    dct:relation [ dct:description "The GAIA-X Policy Rules Conformity Document outlines the normative high-level objectives for service offering providers in areas such as cybersecurity and data protection. Additionally, it defines various attributes used to describe participants, services, and resources within the GAIA-X ecosystem."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:SemanticInteroperabilityAgreementContract ],
        [ dct:description "The GAIA-X Policy Rules Conformity Document defines key elements in a standardized manner to foster interoperability and smooth communication between users. In this context, the specification establishes a common approach for describing services, participants, and resources."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:SemanticAgreementContract ] ;
    dcat:theme "Implementation Governance"@en .

