cssvrsc:449d772a61928d1cdd3940897b7e25adfb553c1947aa38504667c0eaf8a7a7cf a cssv:Specification ;
    dct:relation [ dct:description "The RFC 7641 specification is designed to facilitate the observation of resources on a network, enabling clients to automatically receive updates whenever the state of a resource changes. This is particularly useful for sensors or IoT devices, which may collect information such as temperature, humidity, or other measurements. The specification allows a device to subscribe to a resource on a server so that updates are sent automatically, improving efficiency in data exchange."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataExchangeApplicationComponent ],
        [ dct:description "The RFC 7641 specification is designed to facilitate the observation of resources on a network, enabling clients to automatically receive updates whenever the state of a resource changes. This is particularly useful for sensors or IoT devices, which may collect information such as temperature, humidity, or other measurements. The specification allows a device to subscribe to a resource on a server so that updates are sent automatically, improving efficiency in data exchange."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataExchangeApplicationService ],
        [ dct:description "The RFC 7641 specification is designed to facilitate the observation of resources on a network, such as those provided by sensors or IoT devices. It enables clients to receive automatic notifications whenever a resource changes, thereby avoiding the need for manual updates. This mechanism reduces response time, improves efficiency, and automates the delivery of updates from sensors or other devices."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:SensorDevice ],
        [ dct:description "The RFC 7641 specification is designed to facilitate the updating of the state of information collected by sensors or IoT devices. In this context, an application can connect to a server to receive automatic updates from the sensor, allowing it to operate autonomously and send notifications whenever the state of the collected information changes."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:SmartDeviceDevice ] ;
    dcat:theme "Technology Architecture"@en .

cssvrsc:44f1bdffd784bbc0a93d05ae169fd1a3965afa3abd9b6ba7b40ebccd9282d2d5 a cssv:Specification ;
    dct:relation [ dct:description "The SPDX standard is addressed to improve the exchange of information by using a standardised format for presenting information that ensures that it is consistent across industries and companies. In this sense, the standard provides common formats for organisations and communities to share important data, thereby streamlining and improving compliance, security, and dependability."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataExchangeApplicationComponent ],
        [ dct:description "The SPDX standard is addressed to improve the exchange of information by using a standardised format for presenting information that ensures that it is consistent across industries and companies. In this sense, the standard provides common formats for organisations and communities to share important data, thereby streamlining and improving compliance, security, and dependability."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataExchangeApplicationService ],
        [ dct:description "SPDX allows for the indexation of knowledge about solutions and software packages, licensing and copyright data, which could contribute to the design ofa repository with descriptive data about digital solutions and interoperable solutions."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:SoftwareComponentsCatalogueDataObject ] ;
    dcat:theme "Data Architecture"@en,
        "Technology Architecture"@en .

cssvrsc:459ce55245869fa8d2fe286ec86dfea886241f1366deef90c41db0686c7eab12 a cssv:Specification ;
    dct:relation [ dct:description "Training data is used to train AI/ML models, and to then validate model results. Formalizing and documenting the training data by characterizing the training data content, metadata, data quality, and provenance, and so forth is essential."@en ;
