    dct:relation [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification is intended to facilitate access to and the retrieval of information by enabling the use of queries. This allows users to request information, as well as to update and add new RDF data via SPARQL queries."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataManagementApplicationComponent ],
        [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification is intended to facilitate access to and the retrieval of information by enabling the use of queries. This allows users to request information, as well as to update and add new RDF data via SPARQL queries."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataManagementApplicationService ],
        [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification is designed to facilitate access to resources through the use of queries. In this context, the specification enables users to update and add new data using queries, as well as to retrieve stored data."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataPersistenceApplicationComponent ],
        [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification is designed to facilitate access to resources through the use of queries. In this context, the specification enables users to update and add new data using queries, as well as to retrieve stored data."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataPersistenceApplicationService ],
        [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification can help make data publicly available on the web by using queries to add and update data within RDF graphs hosted on servers. Consequently, this data becomes accessible to other users searching for information."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataPublicationApplicationComponent ],
        [ dct:description "The SPARQL 1.1 Protocol specification can help make data publicly available on the web by using queries to add and update data within RDF graphs hosted on servers. Consequently, this data becomes accessible to other users searching for information."@en ;
            dct:relation eira:DataPublicationApplicationService ] ;
    dcat:theme "Technology Architecture"@en .

